{"id": "EUVD-2026-103474", "enisaUuid": "68ffab1e-f2d7-307f-8869-7b21c508f974", "description": "snac2 before 2.93 contains a heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability in _xs_json_load_lexer() that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to corrupt heap memory by sending JSON strings containing a \\u0000 escape. Attackers can send a single crafted application/activity+json POST to activitypub_post_handler(), which parses it before signature checks, overflowing heap allocations and crashing the server.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:05:15", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://nullenvk.pl/posts/02-snac2-json", "https://gist.github.com/nullenvk/2bf288e2d34cb3d4b7143e61dbf7d90b", "https://codeberg.org/grunfink/snac2/src/tag/2.92/xs_json.h#L283-L285", "https://codeberg.org/grunfink/snac2/commit/ec2c5c2046e0381bc942ec5d0d05ec861fe377e7", "https://codeberg.org/grunfink/snac2/releases/tag/2.93", "https://codeberg.org/grunfink/snac2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/snac2-before-2.93-heap-based-buffer-overflow-via-json-parser-xs-json-load-lexer"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112021", "GHSA-6hv3-2r7g-774j"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e16027b-1a61-3c2b-a1fb-e3133401060b", "product": {"name": "snac2", "vendor": {"name": "grunfink"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.93"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9eae4da1-7bb6-35d9-8241-0ba625ef9b49", "vendor": {"name": "grunfink"}}], "isExploited": false}